<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Revenue Recovery Agent -- Results (seed {{ seed }})</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #1b1f24;
    --muted: #5b6472;
    --line: #dde2e8;
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --panel: #f6f8fa;
    --good: #0f7a3d;
    --bad: #b3261e;
    --accent: #1a56db;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg); line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 0.25rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .pitch { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; }
  .pitch strong.gain { color: var(--good); }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .headline td.agent, .headline th.agent { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .card { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .badge { display: inline-block; padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .badge.disputed { background: #fde8e8; color: var(--bad); }
  .badge.partially_paid { background: #fff4e0; color: #8a5a00; }
  .badge.open { background: #eef1f5; color: var(--muted); }
  .reasons { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .exceptions td.persona { color: var(--muted); }
  .exceptions td.reason { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; }
  .disclaimer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .audit { font-family: "SF Mono", Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .audit td { padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; max-width: 0; }
  .audit td.reason-cell { white-space: normal; max-width: none; }
  .empty { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }
  .win { color: var(--good); font-weight: 600; }
  .lose { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 600; }
  .win-rate { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0.75rem 0 0; }
  .guardrails { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .guardrails li { padding: 0.6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .guardrails li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .guardrails .claim { font-weight: 600; }
  .guardrails .proof { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; margin-top: 0.2rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <h1>Revenue Recovery Agent -- Baseline vs Agent</h1>
  <div class="meta">
    seed {{ seed }} &middot; {{ days }} simulated days &middot; generated {{ generated }}
  </div>

  <p class="pitch">
    Same seeded invoices, same buyer world, two agents. The baseline is a
    dumb 3-fixed-reminder bot (mirrors how Razorpay Payment Links reminders
    behave today). Our agent recovered <strong class="gain">{{ gain }} more</strong>
    with {{ message_delta_phrase }}.
  </p>

  <h2>Headline</h2>
  <table class="headline">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Metric</th><th class="num">Baseline</th><th class="num agent">Agent</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in headline %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.label }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.baseline }}</td>
        <td class="num agent">{{ row.agent }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% if days_to_pay_note %}
  <p class="reasons">{{ days_to_pay_note }}</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Buyer panel -- who needs attention right now</h2>
  <p class="reasons">
    Every buyer who currently has at least one outstanding invoice, worst
    first by total outstanding. Score, confidence and trend are
    engine/score.py's own figures, unchanged; promise reliability counts only
    settled (kept or broken) promises, never one still in flight; response
    rate is replies of any kind (payment, promise, dispute, partial payment)
    against messages sent. A figure the data cannot honestly support says so
    instead of printing a number.
  </p>
  {% if buyer_panel %}
  <table class="exceptions">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Buyer</th><th class="num">Outstanding</th><th class="num">Overdue</th>
        <th class="num">Oldest</th><th class="num">Score</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Trend</th>
        <th>Promise reliability</th><th class="num">Made</th><th class="num">In flight</th>
        <th>Avg days late</th><th class="num">Sent</th><th>Response rate</th>
        <th>Recovery state</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in buyer_panel %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.name }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.outstanding }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.overdue_count }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.oldest_days_overdue }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.score if row.score is not none else "n/a" }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.confidence or "n/a" }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.trend }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.promise_reliability }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.promise_made }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.promise_in_flight }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.avg_days_late or "-" }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.messages_sent }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.response_rate }}</td>
        <td class="reasons">
          {{ row.in_ladder }} in ladder, {{ row.handed_off }} handed off,
          {{ row.stopped }} stopped{% if row.not_yet_due %}, {{ row.not_yet_due }} not yet due{% endif %}
        </td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">No buyer currently has an outstanding balance in this run.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Is this just one lucky seed?</h2>
  {% if multi_seed %}
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Seed</th><th class="num">₹ baseline</th><th class="num">₹ agent</th><th>₹ win</th>
        <th class="num">Days baseline</th><th class="num">Days agent</th><th>Days win</th>
        <th class="num">Malformed invoices</th><th class="num">Superseded promises</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in multi_seed.rows %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.seed }}{{ " (detailed above)" if loop.first }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.baseline_recovered }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.agent_recovered }}</td>
        <td class="{{ 'win' if row.money_win else 'lose' }}">{{ "✓" if row.money_win else "✗" }}</td>
        {% if row.matched_n %}
        <td class="num">{{ row.matched_baseline_days }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.matched_agent_days }}</td>
        <td class="{{ 'win' if row.days_win else 'lose' }}">{{ "✓" if row.days_win else "✗" }}</td>
        {% else %}
        <td class="num empty">n/a</td><td class="num empty">n/a</td><td class="empty">no data</td>
        {% endif %}
        <td class="num">{{ row.malformed_invoices }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.superseded_promise_invoices }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="win-rate">
    Agent won on ₹ recovered in <strong>{{ multi_seed.money_win_rate }}</strong> seeds,
    and on avg days-to-pay (the fair, matched-set comparison) in
    <strong>{{ multi_seed.days_win_rate }}</strong> seeds{% if multi_seed.days_excluded %}
    ({{ multi_seed.days_excluded }} seed(s) excluded -- no invoice was recovered by both runs
    at this window length){% endif %}.
  </p>
  {% if edge_case_note %}
  <p class="win-rate">{{ edge_case_note }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">
    Multi-seed comparison skipped for this run (--extra-seeds ""). Seed {{ seed }} alone is
    shown above and throughout this report.
  </p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Per-rung effectiveness -- the agent's escalation ladder</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Rung</th><th class="num">Invoices contacted</th><th class="num">Recovered at this rung</th><th class="num">Effectiveness</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in per_rung %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.rung }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.invoices_contacted }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.recovered_here }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.effectiveness_pct }}%</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="reasons">
    Escalated to a human, by reason:
    {% if handoff_reasons %}
      {% for reason, count in handoff_reasons %}{{ reason }} ({{ count }}){{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}
    {% else %}<span class="empty">none</span>{% endif %}
    &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Hard-stopped, by reason:
    {% if stop_reasons %}
      {% for reason, count in stop_reasons %}{{ reason }} ({{ count }}){{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}
    {% else %}<span class="empty">none</span>{% endif %}
  </p>

  <h2>Per-reminder effectiveness -- the baseline's fixed schedule</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Attempt</th><th class="num">Invoices contacted</th><th class="num">Recovered at this attempt</th><th class="num">Effectiveness</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in per_attempt %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.attempt }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.invoices_contacted }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.recovered_here }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.effectiveness_pct }}%</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Early warning -- invoices flagged before they went overdue</h2>
  <p class="reasons">
    Rule-based, surfacing only -- no message is ever sent and no legal fact is
    ever stated here, because nothing on this list is legally due yet. An
    invoice is flagged only once at least two of three signals the agent
    already computes look bad: a poor buyer score, a pattern of broken
    promises, or a pattern of that buyer's other invoices going overdue. A
    band, not a probability -- there is no ground truth to validate a
    percentage against.
  </p>
  {% if early_warnings %}
  <table class="exceptions">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Invoice</th><th>Buyer</th><th>Band</th>
        <th class="num">Due in</th><th class="num">Outstanding</th><th>Reasons</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in early_warnings %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.invoice_id }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.buyer_id }}</td>
        <td><span class="badge {{ 'disputed' if row.risk_band == 'high' else 'partially_paid' }}">{{ row.risk_band }}</span></td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.due_in }}d</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.outstanding }}</td>
        <td class="reason">{{ row.reasons }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">No invoice in this run's window triggered an early warning.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Exceptions -- what the agent did NOT recover, and why</h2>
  {% if exceptions %}
  <table class="exceptions">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Invoice</th><th>Buyer</th><th>Persona</th><th>Status</th>
        <th class="num">Outstanding</th><th class="num">Days overdue</th><th>Reason</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in exceptions %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.invoice_id }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.buyer_name }}</td>
        <td class="persona">{{ row.persona }}</td>
        <td><span class="badge {{ row.status }}">{{ row.status }}</span></td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.outstanding }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ row.days_overdue }}</td>
        <td class="reason">{{ row.reason }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">Every invoice was recovered in this run.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Reply safety net -- possible multi-intent replies</h2>
  <p class="reasons">
    One intent is tracked per buyer reply -- a dispute always takes precedence
    over a promise, and the earliest instalment wins over a later one
    (docs/edge_cases.md TC-032, TC-036). These replies still looked, to a
    coarse rule-based check, like they might carry more than that. Nothing
    here changed the recorded intent, date or amount -- it only flags the
    reply for a human to double check.
  </p>
  {% if trip_wires %}
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Invoice</th><th>Flag</th><th>Reply text</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in trip_wires %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.invoice_id }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.flag }}</td>
        <td class="reason">{{ row.reply }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">No reply in this run's window tripped the dispute/multiple-amount safety net.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Audit trail excerpt (last {{ audit_excerpt | length }} entries)</h2>
  {% if audit_excerpt %}
  <div class="card">
    <table class="audit">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Time</th><th>Invoice</th><th>Actor</th><th>Action</th><th>Source</th><th>Reason</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for entry in audit_excerpt %}
        <tr>
          <td>{{ entry.ts }}</td>
          <td>{{ entry.invoice_id or "-" }}</td>
          <td>{{ entry.actor }}</td>
          <td>{{ entry.action }}</td>
          <td>{{ entry.source }}</td>
          <td class="reason-cell">{{ entry.reason }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="reasons">Full trail: audit/audit_log.jsonl (append-only, one JSON object per action).</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="empty">No audit entries found -- run sim/run_sim.py --compare again to regenerate the trail.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Methodology -- how this was guarded against being rigged</h2>
  <ul class="guardrails">
    {% for item in guardrails %}
    <li>
      <div class="claim">{{ item.claim }}</div>
      <div class="proof">{{ item.proof }}</div>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    Synthetic data, generated with --seed {{ seed }}. Legal figures are simplified
    for a demonstration, current as of the date in config/legal.yaml, and are
    not legal advice. Every ₹ figure above traces back to engine/law.py and the
    audit trail; nothing here is estimated or invented.
  </div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
